**Note:** `@SpanMapping(param = "name", …)` uses reflection to look up the original parameter
names. Ensure your application is compiled with `-parameters` (Gradle already sets this for the
OpenInference modules) so those names are retained; otherwise mappings should reference the
synthetic `arg0`, `arg1`, … names generated by the compiler.


Register the tracer at startup to activate annotation-based tracing:

```
import com.arize.instrumentation.OITracer;
import com.arize.instrumentation.OpenInferenceAgent;
import com.arize.instrumentation.annotation.OpenInferenceAgentInstaller;
// Install ByteBuddy agent BEFORE loading any annotated classes
OpenInferenceAgentInstaller.install();
Tracer otelTracer = GlobalOpenTelemetry.getTracer("my-app");
OITracer tracer = new OITracer(otelTracer);
OpenInferenceAgent.register(tracer);
```
Build the annotation agent JAR (which now advertises `Premain-Class` / `Agent-Class`
entries pointing at `OpenInferenceAgentInstaller`) with:

```
cd java
./gradlew :instrumentation:openinference-instrumentation-annotation:jar
```
The resulting artifact lives under
`java/instrumentation/openinference-instrumentation-annotation/build/libs/`. You can run any
application with annotation tracing enabled by passing the jar to `-javaagent`:

```
java -javaagent:./java/instrumentation/openinference-instrumentation-annotation/build/libs/openinference-instrumentation-annotation.jar \
     -cp your-app.jar com.example.Main
```
The agent automatically installs ByteBuddy and wires the same `OpenInferenceAgentInstaller`
logic that's available for runtime attach. You still need to register an `OITracer` during
application startup so spans have an OpenTelemetry exporter.

Need a concrete reference app? Check out `java/examples/annotation-example`, which shows the
annotation instrumentation in action (both via runtime attach and with `-javaagent`).

For more control, use the `TracedSpan` API directly with try-with-resources:

```
import com.arize.instrumentation.OITracer;
import com.arize.instrumentation.trace.*;
Tracer otelTracer = GlobalOpenTelemetry.getTracer("my-app");
OITracer tracer = new OITracer(otelTracer);
try (AgentSpan agent = AgentSpan.start(tracer, "qa-agent")) {
    agent.setInput("What is OpenInference?");
    agent.setAgentName("qa-agent");
    try (LLMSpan llm = LLMSpan.start(tracer, "generate")) {
        llm.setInput("What is OpenInference?");
        llm.setModelName("gpt-4o");
        String answer = callLLM("What is OpenInference?");
        llm.setOutput(answer);
        llm.setTokenCountTotal(150);
    }
    agent.setOutput("OpenInference is a tracing standard for AI apps.");
}
```
- `OTEL_INSTRUMENTATION_LANGCHAIN4J_ENABLED`: Enable/disable LangChain4j auto-instrumentation (default: true)

